  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong dark technical art direction, disciplined cyan/red semantics, and a clear desktop hero-to-evidence hierarchy. However, tablet and especially mobile become overly dense: metadata and body copy are extremely small, rows turn into tall repetitive blocks, and the comparison/detail panel produces a long monotonous scroll. The mobile/tablet header visibly truncates navigation without a polished continuation cue, while the mobile brand label and red-mode action disappear. Contrast verification is also incomplete for header links.",
    "fix": "Raise small-text sizes and contrast, compress mobile transaction rows into a clearer summary pattern, strengthen spacing between detail sections, and replace the clipped header rail with an explicit overflow/menu treatment that preserves branding and the red-mode action.",
